  "id": "sat",
  "term": "SAT",
  "definition": "SAT, or Sonic Augmentation Technology, is described as a passive auditory method informed by polyvagal theory. It is based on the idea that emotional and bodily difficulties can relate to atypical autonomic regulation, and that healthy functioning depends on flexible coordination among interacting physiological systems rather than any one system alone.",
